0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"130px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535011 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "530f8a57-b248-5ddf-8ae9-a8b808f3a729" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535011 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+2)}\\,x(-2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2)) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2))\\, \\\\ \\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535092 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535092 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "01dd852f-2929-5c79-b2c7-9966a69ca50b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535092 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186311561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535096 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535096 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1241689c-e056-52b5-b26f-3355c23157a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535096 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186535011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535115 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "94ec5f0a-352f-5ac0-bc02-f9deb9d28d5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535115 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535127 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535127 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c7e18732-59fb-5584-9670-78b1b3e4c537" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535127 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186311712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535137 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535137 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "df50ea20-ddc6-5750-beca-6ed839b9bdcd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535137 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229657 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
